Parts that belong to others, used under their own terms:

- The people's bodies, skins, hair, eyes and ready-made outfits (in the people
  folders) come from MakeHuman assets released as CC0 (public domain).
- Many of the people's moves (walking, standing, and most emotes and dances) are
  made from the Carnegie Mellon University motion capture database
  (mocap.cs.cmu.edu), free to use but not to resell.
  The database was created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.
- Ordinal theory (first sat, degree, rarity) follows ord, which is CC0.
- Live Bitcoin data comes from the public services of mempool.space, ordpool.space,
  ordinals.com and ordiscan.com, and their back-ups (mempool.emzy.de, mempool.ninja,
  mempool.bitaroo.net, blockstream.info, static.unisat.io, ordinalswallet.com and
  ord.xverse.app), which are not part of this work. Bitcoin's own data is public.
- Live Dogecoin data comes from the public services of thedoginalsexplorer.com,
  BitPay's Bitcore (api.bitcore.io), Blockchair and Doggy Market (cdn.doggy.market),
  which are not part of this work. Dogecoin's own data is public.
- Inscriptions shown in the portal belong to their own creators.
- The Collection Check's Goosinals example uses inscription IDs from Ordinals Wallet's
  collection list.

